{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Fq9M19xVQk1A7jcekuYCPt", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/george-brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://parks.canada.ca/culture/designation/lieu-site/maison-george-brown-house\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.canada.ca/fr/parcs-canada/nouvelles/2016/08/lieu-historique-national-de-la-maison-george-brown.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://pc.gc.ca/culture/designation/lieu-site/maison-george-brown-house\"}, {\"url\": \"https://development.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/article/george-brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.canada.ca/en/parks-canada/news/2016/08/george-brown-house-national-historic-site.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/1911_Encyclop%C3%A6dia_Britannica/Brown,_George\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.britannica.com/print/article/81515\"}, {\"url\": \"https://wehd.com/bios/George_Brown.html\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:34:14.642Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "George Brown 1818-1880 refused 1875", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01VVsQU8maN2jYJrxYsvk7va", "content": [{"title": "george brown", "url": "https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/george-brown"}, {"title": "George Brown House National Historic Site", "url": "https://parks.canada.ca/culture/designation/lieu-site/maison-george-brown-house"}, {"title": "Lieu historique national de la maison George Brown", "url": "https://www.canada.ca/fr/parcs-canada/nouvelles/2016/08/lieu-historique-national-de-la-maison-george-brown.html"}, {"title": "George Brown House National Historic Site", "url": "https://pc.gc.ca/culture/designation/lieu-site/maison-george-brown-house"}, {"title": "george brown", "url": "https://development.thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/article/george-brown"}, {"title": "George Brown House National Historic Site", "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/parks-canada/news/2016/08/george-brown-house-national-historic-site.html"}, {"title": "Jump to content", "url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/1911_Encyclop%C3%A6dia_Britannica/Brown,_George"}, {"title": "George Brown", "url": "https://www.britannica.com/print/article/81515"}, {"title": "George Brown", "url": "https://wehd.com/bios/George_Brown.html"}]}, "The search confirms that George Brown (1818–1880), the Toronto Globe publisher and Father of Confederation, turned down the Ontario lieutenant governorship in 1875.\n\n- **The 1875 refusal:** The Canadian Encyclopedia says he declined the Ontario post that year, and also declined a knighthood offered in 1879 (Brown refused the position of lieutenant-governor of Ontario in 1875 and an offer of knighthood in 1879.). The Parks Canada plaque for his former home gives the same two refusals (He refused both the lieutenant governorship of Ontario (1875) and a knighthood (1879)).\n- **Reason:** Parks Canada says he preferred to keep an independent public voice as a newspaper editor rather than hold office. The 1911 Britannica entry adds that he then focused on the Globe and his Bow Park model farm near Brantford (devoting himself to the Globe and to a model farm at Bow Park near Brantford).\n- **Death:** Sources agree he was shot by a former Globe employee in 1880, but they differ on the date. Britannica says he died on 9 May 1880 (died May 9, 1880, Toronto, Ontario, Canada). The 1911 Britannica gives the shooting as 25 March 1880, with death on 9 May. One Parks Canada page gives his death as 1881, which conflicts with the other sources."], "durationSeconds": 5.462977917, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Fq9M19xVQk1A7jcekuYCPt", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
